// Punar: nobody sets this machine's clock through timedated.
//
// WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. Privilege grants and pending approvals (M9) expire by
// the wall clock: Grant::is_live and ApprovalEnvelope::has_lapsed in
// crates/punar-common/src/approval.rs compare it with `expires_at`. Step the
// clock back and an elevated grant outlives the 1-60 minute window the person
// approved, and an approval stays answerable after it should have lapsed.
// systemd ships the three actions below as auth_admin_keep, so any account
// that can answer an administrator prompt could move the clock, and every
// expiry with it.
//
// THE DECISION. NO, for every subject. Not a password prompt, because a prompt
// is a yes to whoever can get one answered:
//   * set-time      — step the wall clock to any instant.
//   * set-ntp       — turn synchronization off, so a clock moved by any other
//                     route stays wrong.
//   * set-local-rtc — read the hardware clock as local time, which moves the
//                     wall clock by the zone's offset at the next boot.
//
// WHAT THIS DOES NOT DO, stated so nobody reads more into it:
//   * set-timezone is DELIBERATELY ABSENT. A zone changes how the instant is
//     shown, not which instant it is, and expiry compares UTC; the
//     time.timezone capability and the network-provided zone keep working.
//   * Root is unaffected. timedated skips polkit for a caller that holds
//     CAP_SYS_ADMIN, so a root shell can still `timedatectl set-time`. This
//     closes the unprivileged path; it does not claim to stop root.
//   * The network's path to the clock is closed separately (UseNTP=no in
//     usr/lib/systemd/network/*.network), and Punar's own root services lose
//     the power to set it with ProtectClock=yes.
//   * The dev profile adds nothing here. The CI desktop image (profiles
//     desktop,dev) carries this same file, and none of its checks sets the
//     clock through timedated.
polkit.addRule(function (action, subject) {
    switch (action.id) {
    case "org.freedesktop.timedate1.set-time":
    case "org.freedesktop.timedate1.set-ntp":
    case "org.freedesktop.timedate1.set-local-rtc":
        return polkit.Result.NO;
    }
    return polkit.Result.NOT_HANDLED;
});
